OpenPianos data license
========================

The OpenPianos dataset is dedicated to the public domain under

    Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0)
    Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

To the extent possible under law, the OpenPianos contributors have waived all
copyright and related or neighboring rights to the OpenPianos dataset. You may
copy, modify, distribute, and use it, including for commercial purposes, without
asking permission.


Attribution (a request, not a requirement)
------------------------------------------

CC0 waives the legal requirement to attribute. We nonetheless *ask* that reusers
credit "OpenPianos" with a link, as a community norm — the same way Wikidata does.
It costs you nothing and helps the commons grow.


IMPORTANT — third-party source data
-----------------------------------

OpenPianos aggregates from multiple sources. Some sources carry their own licenses
that OpenPianos CANNOT override:

- OpenStreetMap data is licensed ODbL and MAY NOT be relicensed as CC0. OSM is
  therefore used only as a LEAD for verification/discovery, or kept in a clearly
  separated, ODbL-attributed layer — never mixed into the CC0 core.
- pianos.pub and other partner data are included only with the source's explicit
  permission to redistribute under these terms.

Every record's provenance (its `Source` and license) is preserved in the data, so
reusers can always see what may be redistributed and under which terms. When in
doubt about a specific record, check its source's license before redistributing.


Code
----

Software in the OpenPianos repositories (the `api`, `explorer`, etc.) is licensed
separately under MIT unless a repository states otherwise. This file covers the
DATA.
